<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Thrum Flow collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere. There is no
       network code in the target at all: no analytics, no crash reporter, no
       account, no server. Both of the arrays below are therefore empty, and that
       is a statement of fact rather than a default left in place.

       The one entry that is here is required whether or not anything is
       collected. `Shared/Flow.swift` writes `flow.lastKey` to UserDefaults so a
       relaunch cannot open in the key the last session was in — a passive app is
       killed between listens far more often than it is stopped, so without it
       every session would be able to repeat the last one. UserDefaults is on
       Apple's required-reason list, and CA92.1 is the reason that fits exactly:
       information accessible only to this app, never shared with anything.

       Nothing else in the target touches a required-reason API. The taste
       database is an ordinary file written with `Data.write(to:options:.atomic)`
       in Application Support; no file *timestamps* are read, no disk space is
       queried, and no boot time or active-keyboard information is used. If any
       of that changes, this file has to change with it — a missing declaration
       is ITMS-91053 on upload, not a warning you find later. -->
  <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
  <false/>
  <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
  <array/>
  <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
  <array/>
  <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
      <array>
        <string>CA92.1</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
